- a. The insurer shall provide adequate resources to the Appointed Actuary; 

- b. In order to build up or develop sufficient actuarial expertise, life insurers shall have at least two actuaries and General/Standalone Health insurers shall have at least one actuary in addition to Appointed Actuary for pricing and valuation purposes within such period   as notified by the Authority from time to time; 

- c. The insurer shall ensure that different functions of the insurer provide adequate support to the Appointed Actuary in discharging his or her duties and obligations; 

- d. The insurer shall ensure that the Appointed Actuary does not simultaneously perform   the role of Chief Risk Officer of the insurer defined as per the extant provisions of Corporate Governance Guidelines issued by the Authority. The Chief Risk Officer however may preferably be an Actuary independent of the Appointed Actuary. 

